<title>USA: Fed seen adding reserves via overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed seen adding reserves via overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve is expected to add temporary reserves to the U.S. banking system on Tuesday via overnight system repurchase agreements, market analysts said.</p>
<p>At 1100 EDT/1500 GMT, federal funds were firm at 5-1/2 percent, above the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
